WEBVTT

00:00.760 --> 00:09.000
Yu Gong slandered his sovereign and emperor; his crime deserves death ten thousand times. Yet Father is renowned for benevolence—if you spare his life and exile him to the frontier, it would serve as an exemplary act.

00:09.720 --> 00:17.680
First, it warns the world never to defy imperial authority; second, it displays Father's magnanimity toward outspoken subjects to all under heaven.

00:18.160 --> 00:24.500
As the ancients taught: "Spare the nest of the crow, and the phoenix will descend; withhold execution for outspoken words, and honest counsel will freely flow."

00:25.000 --> 00:30.500
My second son... the moral theories in your history books cannot simply be blindly brandished in the real world.

00:32.000 --> 00:45.000
Do you think I would not wish to be celebrated as a sage ruler for the ages? But our house has barely stood firm south of the river for a handful of years! Countless great aristocratic clans watch our every breath like wolves—I cannot afford a single mistake.

00:46.920 --> 00:54.000
Putting him to death may not be the deed of an enlightened sovereign; yet if I spare him, every scholar in the realm will feel emboldened to recklessly challenge the throne!
